window.NARRATIVES={"1": "Sprayed a custom wordlist (NCSC 100k most-used passwords) across 8 known Stark users against Winterfell and Castelblack. **brandon.stark:iseedeadpeople** succeeded on line 26028 of the list. This triggered 302 failed logon events (4625) and 25 burst alerts (rule 60204, level 10) — the SIEM **did** detect the spray.", "2": "With brandon's domain credentials, enumerated SYSVOL/NETLOGON shares on Winterfell. Found **secret.ps1** containing `jeor.mormont : _L0ngCl@w_` in cleartext. Wazuh logged 29 NTLM logons (brandon → Winterfell), but share-access auditing (5140/5145) was off — the actual file read is invisible.", "3": "Ran **crackmapexec ldap --users** as brandon.stark against Winterfell. Enumerated all domain users; **samwell.tarly**'s AD description field literally contained `(Password : Heartsbane)` — readable by any authenticated user. BloodHound later confirmed this in the graph data.", "4": "Used jeor.mormont's plaintext password to authenticate to Castelblack via SMB. CrackMapExec returned **(Pwn3d!)** — jeor is a local Administrator. BloodHound shows LAPS=disabled on this host (shared local admin). Wazuh logged 15 NTLM remote-admin events (rule 92652) from .100.", "5": "Dumped LSA secrets on Castelblack using **secretsdump.py** as jeor.mormont (local admin). The LSA secret `_SC_MSSQL$SQLEXPRESS` held sql_svc's password in **cleartext**: `YouWillNotKerboroast1ngMeeeeee`. Wazuh: 2 failed sql_svc logons (4625) then 9 successful (60106).", "6": "Authenticated to MSSQL on Castelblack as sql_svc (sysadmin). Enabled **xp_cmdshell** and executed OS commands (`whoami` returned `north\\sql_svc`). This confirms RCE capability on the member server. sql_svc is also Kerberoastable (SPN present, though password already known).", "7": "Ran **bloodhound-python** as brandon.stark against Winterfell, collecting All (users, groups, computers, containers, GPOs, OUs, domains). The graph revealed: **SAMWELL.TARLY** has GenericWrite/WriteOwner/WriteDacl on GPO **STARKWALLPAPER** (C0CB1EC9-…), which is linked to the Domain Controllers OU → path to DC local admin.", "8": "Abused the GPO write with **pyGPOAbuse.py** as samwell.tarly. Injected a scheduled immediate task: `net localgroup administrators samwell.tarly /add` on the DC. Winterfell executed it, granting samwell local admin. CrackMapExec confirmed **(Pwn3d!)** on 192.168.56.11. **Wazuh: 0 events** — object-change (5136) and task-creation (4698) auditing are off. Complete blind spot.", "9": "With samwell as local admin on the DC, ran **secretsdump.py -just-dc** against Winterfell. Performed child **DCSync** (DRSUAPI replication from non-DC). Retrieved all north.sevenkingdoms.local hashes: **goadmin** (DA), **krbtgt** (502), **SEVENKINGDOMS$** trust key (1106), all user NTLMs + AES keys. **Wazuh: 0 events** — Directory-Service-Access auditing (4662) is disabled. The pivotal credential theft was invisible.", "10": "Tested cross-trust auth: **Pass-the-Hash** with north\\goadmin's NTLM (dbd13e1c…) against the root DC Kingslanding. CrackMapExec: `[+]` (authenticated) but **not (Pwn3d!)** — goadmin from the child has no local admin on the root. The trust allows auth (SID filtering **disabled**), but more is needed for root DA. Wazuh: 47× 4624 + 44× rule 92652 for goadmin on Kingslanding.", "11": "Escalated to forest admin with **raiseChild.py** (Impacket 0.13.1). Used child goadmin + plaintext password `NgtI75cKV+Pu`. raiseChild forged a TGT with the child krbtgt, injecting **ExtraSid** (Enterprise Admins …-519), then performed DRSUAPI against the root DC. Retrieved root **goadmin** (c66d7202…, cleartext `8dCT-DJjgScp`) + root **krbtgt** hashes. The foreign EA SID grants full forest control.", "12": "Performed root **DCSync** with `secretsdump.py -just-dc` as sevenkingdoms.local\\goadmin (password `8dCT-DJjgScp`) against Kingslanding. Dumped the entire root NTDS: all Lannister/Baratheon/NORTH$/etc. hashes. **Full forest takeover**. Wazuh: **0 events** — like the child, 4662 auditing is off on the root DC. The final credential exfiltration was unlogged.", "13": "Created **persistence** backdoor via WMI: `net user KINGHODOR holdthatdoor /add /domain` + added to Enterprise Admins & Domain Admins. Wazuh logged the account creation (4720, rule 60109, level 8) and enablement (4738, 60110), but the **group additions (4728/4756) produced 0 events** — Security Group Management auditing is off. The dangerous privilege grant was invisible.", "14": "Verified KINGHODOR access: `smbclient //192.168.56.10/C$` succeeded. Ran DCSync as KINGHODOR — confirmed full replication rights. The persistence account has unrestricted EA+DA in the forest.", "15": "LDAP query confirmed: `CN=KINGHODOR,…` is a **member of Enterprise Admins**. The backdoor is durable and survives goadmin password rotation. Forest compromise is complete and persistent."};
